From d1cd44306f1d9dc4052505cc3c4ec5fc2308b73e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:40:11 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(turning): lathe chucks fit to the stock in the
 dialog, grip inside, stepped jaws

The Add accessory dialog offers "Fit to the stock" for the 3-jaw, 4-jaw
and collet chuck (the existing OnStock placement), ticked when the
setup's stock is round. A jaw chuck gains a grip direction (outside or
inside, the inside jaw's face the circumscribed arc of the bore it opens
into) and stepped jaws (step_height, step_depth; a fitted stock sits on
the step). Every impossible figure is refused by name, and a stock fit
with an inside grip is refused: the stock does not state a bore.

MCP: add_accessory and set_accessory take grip and the step figures;
the camcraft-mcp skill row lists the chuck kinds, fit_to_stock and
grip (PROCESS_VERSION 77). Projects saved before read as plain outside
jaws; the default chuck's mesh is unchanged.

Pinned by sim lathe_chuck_jaws (envelopes, volumes, refusals, old
files), app lathe_chuck (inside-grip and stepped jaws block the post;
the fit seats the stock on the step), app mcp_accessory and the ui
fixture_accessory tests (chuck_dialog_offers_fit_to_the_stock).

Refs #1468

